🐛 Describe the bug
Exporting to_dense() node to FX graph fails for sparse compressed
When I try the following FX graph sparsity export added to the existing test/export/test_sparse.py test
class ToDenseNet(torch.nn.Module):
    def forward(self, x):
        return x.to_dense()
...
    @parametrize("dtype", DTYPES)
    @parametrize("itype", ITYPES)
    @all_sparse_layouts("layout")
    def test_todensenet(self, dtype, itype, layout):
        net = ToDenseNet()
        for sparse_input in self.generate_simple_inputs(
            layout,
            device="cpu",
            dtype=dtype,
            index_dtype=itype,
        ):
            result = net(sparse_input)
            # Build the traced graph.
            prog = torch.export.export(net, (sparse_input,))
            # Test arg/todense/output.
            for i, node in enumerate(prog.graph.nodes):
                meta = node.meta.get("val", None)
                if i == 0:
                    self.assertEqualMeta(meta, sparse_input)
                elif i == 1:
                    self.assertEqualMeta(meta, result)
                else:
                    self.assertEqual(meta, None)

Then this succeeds for all the sparse coo cases, but fails for the sparse compressed cases, such as:
  python test/export/test_sparse.py TestSparseProp.test_todensenet_int64_int64_SparseCSR

I looked into the calling pattern, and it seems to break in the interpreter  when calling to_dense()  during symbolic analysis. Even though the self argument is of type class 'torch._subclasses.functional_tensor.FunctionalTensor', the generic to_dense() function in C++ land queries the layout using layout() -> virtual call -> TensorImpl::layout_impl() (which asserts) rather than the FunctionalTensorWrapper::layout_impl() which would relay the call to the proper sparse compressed layout.
  File "/usr/local/google/home/ajcbik/PYTORCH2/pytorch/torch/fx/interpreter.py", line 303, in call_method
    return getattr(self_obj, target)(*args_tail, **kwargs)
           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
RuntimeError: layout_impl is only implemented for TensorImpl subclasses.

I tried to debug this for a bit now, but I don't understand why sparse coo takes the right path, but compressed sparse does not. Any pointers here?
