🐛 Describe the bug
I suspect that inductor might not be fusing float8-related code which could be fused.  Specifically, in user code, we have
# user code - forward
f8_activation = to_float8(...)
f8_input_t_c_t = f8_tensor.t().contiguous().t()  # for backward
torch._scaled_mm(f8_activation, ...)

# aot_autograd captures all of the above in the same forward graph, but inductor does not fuse the t().contigous().t() into the kernel which creates the original float8 activation

relevant lines of aot_graph and fusion logs (from paste below)
// aot_graph extract

// convert f8_activation to float8_e4m3fn dtype
convert_element_type: "f8e4m3fn[4096, 4096][4096, 1]cuda:0" = torch.ops.prims.convert_element_type.default(clamp_max, torch.float8_e4m3fn);

// a bit later, reshape-contiguous-reshape
permute_2: "f8e4m3fn[4096, 4096][1, 4096]cuda:0" = torch.ops.aten.permute.default(convert_element_type, [1, 0]);
clone_1: "f8e4m3fn[4096, 4096][4096, 1]cuda:0" = torch.ops.aten.clone.default(permute_2, memory_format = torch.contiguous_format);
permute_3: "f8e4m3fn[4096, 4096][1, 4096]cuda:0" = torch.ops.aten.permute.default(clone_1, [1, 0]);

// then, relevant excerpt from inductor fusion logs
fuse_nodes_once, candidates:
...
SchedulerNode(name='op6'), Pointwise(['[4096, 4096]', 'origins=OrderedSet([clamp_min, convert_element_type, mul, clamp_max])'])
...
SchedulerNode(name='op9'), Pointwise(['[4096, 4096]', 'origins=OrderedSet([clone_1])'])
...
cannot fuse op6 with op9: no shared data

// adding some additional logs to the function which scores the memory fusions:
// op6.reads
OrderedSet([MemoryDep('primals_3', c0, {c0: 16777216}, None), MemoryDep('primals_2', 0, {}, None)])
// op6.writes
OrderedSet([MemoryDep('buf6', c0, {c0: 16777216}, None)])                                          
// op9.reads
OrderedSet([MemoryDep('buf6', c0 + 4096*c1, {c0: 4096, c1: 4096}, None)])                          
// op9.writes
OrderedSet([MemoryDep('buf6', c0 + 4096*c1, {c0: 4096, c1: 4096}, None)])                          

4096^2 = 16777216, and the buffer name matches.  Is it intended behavior that inductor is not fusing the two sets of nodes above?
